No signals and no child processes (docs/gpu3d.md G1; CLAUDE.md,
*Compatibility inside a process yes, at system level never*). A Kosmos
process receives no signals and cannot fork or exec. LLVM's Support
library has its Unix half for both, so on Kosmos:

- signals and running another program are files of their own,
  lib/Support/Kosmos/Signals.inc and Program.inc, chosen where Unix's
  would be: nothing is delivered, a program cannot be started and says
  so, and what means something without either - callbacks run on a fatal
  error, files removed when the interrupt handlers run, text and binary
  modes - is kept;
- crash recovery keeps setjmp's half with no handlers to install;
- the watchdog sets no alarm, core files are not prevented because none
  are written, a descriptor closes without a signal mask, and the
  terminal's width is not asked of an ioctl Kosmos refuses;
- <sys/wait.h> and <dlfcn.h> are not included: no children, and no
  dynamic loader (LLVM already does without one when HAVE_DLOPEN is
  unset).

